{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Disclaimer: This video was produced in collaboration\nwith the US Census Bureau and fact-checked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2500,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by Census Bureau scientists; any opinions\nand errors are my own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4500,
    "dDurationMs": 4139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every ten years the US Census Bureau surveys\nthe American population - the ambitious goal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8639,
    "dDurationMs": 3781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is to count every person currently living\nin the entire United States of America and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12420,
    "dDurationMs": 3799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collect information about them like age, sex,\nrace and ethnicity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16219,
    "dDurationMs": 4161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The whole purpose of doing surveys like the\ncensus (and many other big medical or demographic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20380,
    "dDurationMs": 3909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "surveys) is to be able to get an overall,\nquantitative picture of a particular population"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24289,
    "dDurationMs": 2301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- how many people live in Minnesota?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26590,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or Mississippi?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27590,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What’s their average age?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28670,
    "dDurationMs": 3949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And how do these things differ in different\nplaces, or by sex, or race?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32619,
    "dDurationMs": 4401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The results of the US Census are of particular\npolitical relevance since they’re used to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37020,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "determine the numbers of seats that different\nstates get in the US House of Representatives"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40550,
    "dDurationMs": 4751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as well as the boundaries of legislative districts\nfrom Congress down to city councils, but big"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45301,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "surveys are also useful for understanding\nlots of other issues, too . The problem, of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49481,
    "dDurationMs": 4419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "course, is that the Census (like many other\nmedical and demographic studies) is supposed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53900,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be private."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55100,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, no one outside the Census Bureau is\nsupposed to be able to look at just the published"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59120,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "statistics about the US population demographics\nand definitively figure out that there’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63500,
    "dDurationMs": 4929,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a white married male 31-year old with no kids\nliving in my neighborhood (that’s me)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68429,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The census bureau is supposed to keep my information\nconfidential."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72109,
    "dDurationMs": 3050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they’re supposed to keep the information\nof every single other person living in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75159,
    "dDurationMs": 2341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "United States confidential, too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77500,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is a tall order, because how can you\nkeep everyone’s information entirely confidential"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81960,
    "dDurationMs": 3509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while still saying anything at all based on\nthat information?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85469,
    "dDurationMs": 1911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The short answer is that you can’t."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87380,
    "dDurationMs": 4599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There’s an inherent tradeoff between publishing\nsomething you learn from a survey and maintaining"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91979,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the privacy of the participants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94049,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It might seem like you could just remove people’s\nnames from the spreadsheet, or only publish"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97899,
    "dDurationMs": 2271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "summaries like averages and totals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100170,
    "dDurationMs": 4509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it’s easy to reconnect names to datasets\nusing powerful computers, and there’s a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104679,
    "dDurationMs": 2870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematical theorem that guarantees that\nif you do a study, every single piece of accurate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107549,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "information that you release, however small\nit seems, will inherently violate the privacy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112149,
    "dDurationMs": 2131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the participants to some degree violate\nthe privacy of the participants in that study"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114280,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to some degree."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115280,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the more information you publicly release,\nthe more you violate the individual privacies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118590,
    "dDurationMs": 1309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the participants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119899,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how do you quantitatively measure something\nnebulous like loss of privacy, and then how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124779,
    "dDurationMs": 1331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do you protect it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126110,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand how to measure privacy, it’s\nhelpful to start by imagining how somebody"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129950,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would try use published results (from a study)\nand piece together the private information"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133850,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the people surveyed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135080,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They could just try to steal or gain direct\naccess to the private information itself , which,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139200,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of course, can’t be protected against mathematically\n- it requires good computer security, or physical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143880,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "defenses, so we won’t consider it here!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146130,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The kind of privacy attack we can defend against\nmathematically is an attack that looks at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150270,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "publicly published statistics and then applies\nbrute force computational power to imagine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154760,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all possible combinations of answers the participants\ncould have given to see which ones are the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159270,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most plausible - that is, which ones fit the\npublished statistics the best."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163830,
    "dDurationMs": 3190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine checking all possible combinations\nof letters and numbers for a password until"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167020,
    "dDurationMs": 8470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of them works, except instead of letters\nand numbers it’s checking all possible “combinations-of-the-answers-that-330-million-people-could-give-on-their-census-questionnaires”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175490,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to see which combinations come closest to\nthe publicly published figures for average"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179150,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "age, racial breakdown, and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181640,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The more closely a potential combination of\nanswers matches the published figures , the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185880,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more promising a candidate it is (from the\nattacker’s perspective)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189540,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The more poorly it matches, the lower their\nlevel of certainty."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192930,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a small example, if there are 7 people\nliving in a particular area and you tell me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197010,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that four are female, four like ice cream,\nfour are married adults, three of the ice"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201130,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cream lovers are female, and if you also give\nme the mean and median ages for all of these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205100,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "categories, then I can perfectly reconstruct\nthe exact ages, sex, and ice cream preference"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210220,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of everyone involved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211220,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would start with the 3 ice cream loving\nfemales; even though there are hundreds of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215180,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thousands of possible combinations of ages\nfor three people, only a small fraction of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219300,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those - 36, in fact - are plausible - they’re\nin the right combination to give a median"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224380,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "age of 36 and a mean age of 36 and two thirds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227640,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the same thing works for the four females\noverall - there are almost 10 million possible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231890,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combinations of ages they could have , but\nonly 24 age combinations that are consistent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236490,
    "dDurationMs": 5750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a median of 30, a mean of 33.5, AND with\nat least one of the plausible age combinations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242240,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the three ice-cream lovers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243880,
    "dDurationMs": 4559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Continuing on with this kind of deduction\nleads to a single plausible (and perfect)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248439,
    "dDurationMs": 4321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reconstruction of all of the ages, sexes,\nand ice-cream preferences of the people involved;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252760,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a 100% violation of privacy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255450,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If, however, you didn’t list how many of\nthe ice cream lovers were female, there would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258870,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead be two plausible possibilities, so\nI would be less certain which was the true"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263130,
    "dDurationMs": 8640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combination of ages and genders and ice cream\npreferences."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271770,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the potential level of certainty of an\nattacker is precisely how we measure the loss"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275620,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of privacy from publishing results of a study."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278770,
    "dDurationMs": 5519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If all possible combinations of ages and sexes\nand so on are similarly plausible, then an"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284289,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "attacker can’t distinguish between them\nvery well and so privacy is well protected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289009,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if a small number of the possibilities\nare significantly more plausible than the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292639,
    "dDurationMs": 4291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rest, they stand out - and precisely because\nthey stand out on plausibility, they’re"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296930,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also likely to be close to the truth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298849,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to protect privacy, all possibilities need\nto seem similarly plausible, or at least there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304509,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can’t be plausibility peaks that are too\nconspicuous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307879,
    "dDurationMs": 4611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The potential for plausibility peaks is quantified\nmathematically by measuring the maximum slope"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312490,
    "dDurationMs": 4049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the graph - if the slope never gets too\nsteep, then you can’t have any sharp peaks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316539,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of highly plausible possibilities that stand\nout.But how do we publish statistics in a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321129,
    "dDurationMs": 4941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "way that limits the maximum slope (and possible\npeaks) on the plausibilities plot?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326070,
    "dDurationMs": 4279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In practice, the best way to limit an attacker’s\nability to confidently choose one scenario"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330349,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the other is to randomly change, or “jitter”,\nthe published values."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334499,
    "dDurationMs": 4411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, for example, rolling a die and adding\nthat number to the average age reported for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338910,
    "dDurationMs": 1559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ice-cream lovers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340469,
    "dDurationMs": 3571,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jittering the published results in a mathematically\nrigorous way puts a limit on the slope of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344040,
    "dDurationMs": 3739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the plausibility graph, and thus makes it\nharder for any particular possibilities to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347779,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stand out above the rest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349729,
    "dDurationMs": 4121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jittering results might also seem like lying,\nbut as long as the size of the adjustment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353850,
    "dDurationMs": 3779,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn’t big enough to make any significant\nchanges to conclusions people draw from the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357629,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "survey, then it’s considered worth it for\nthe privacy protection."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360069,
    "dDurationMs": 4111,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, imagine I want to give you a\nsense of my age while keeping my true age"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364180,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "secret."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365180,
    "dDurationMs": 5690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If I just told you my age, obviously there’s\njust one plausible possibility - 31!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370870,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But suppose instead that I secretly pulled\na number between minus 5 and 5 out of a hat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375210,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and added it to my age before telling you\n. In this case, all you know is that my true"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379610,
    "dDurationMs": 5429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "age is somewhere within 5 years of the number\nI told you, but you don’t know my age exactly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385039,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "My privacy has been preserved, though only\nto a certain degree because you can be confident"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389289,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I’m not 20 and not 40."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391479,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To protect my age more, I’d have to pull\na number between, say, -10 and 10 out of a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395879,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hat and add it to my age - this increases\nthe number of plausible possibilities - that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400599,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is, the possible true ages that COULD have\nresulted in the number I told you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404569,
    "dDurationMs": 7070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It also increases your uncertainty about my\nactual age - the tradeoff for privacy is inaccuracy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411639,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If I wanted you to know my age within a year,\nI could only pull a number between -1 and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416169,
    "dDurationMs": 5610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1 out of the hat.In general, the idea is this:\nmore privacy means you get less accuracy . Less"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421779,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "privacy means you can have more accuracy . When\nyou publish results, hopefully there’s a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427559,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sweet spot where you can share something useful\nwhile still sufficiently maintaining peoples’"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431979,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "privacy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432979,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And simultaneously maintaining decent privacy\nand decent accuracy gets easier and easier"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437749,
    "dDurationMs": 1540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with larger datasets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439289,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like how as I add more noise to this image,\nyou can still get the general picture even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443289,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "once you’ve lost any hope of telling the\ntrue original value of a particular pixel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447319,
    "dDurationMs": 5041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, to protect people’s privacy, we can\nand should randomly jitter published statistics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452360,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(which the US Census, for example, has been\ndoing since the 1970s)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456310,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, there’s a subtlety - you can’t\njust add any old random noise however frequently"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461150,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you want - if I simply add different random\nnoise to this picture a bunch of times different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464860,
    "dDurationMs": 3019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times, once you take the average of all of\nthe noisy images you basically get back the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467879,
    "dDurationMs": 3481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "original clean image - you don’t want this\nhappening to your data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471360,
    "dDurationMs": 4269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, there’s a whole field of computer science\ndedicated to figuring out how to add the least"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475629,
    "dDurationMs": 4970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "possible amount of noise to get both the most\nprivacy and the most accuracy, and to future-proof"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480599,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the publication of data so that when you publish\nmultiple jittered statistics about people,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484259,
    "dDurationMs": 3171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those statistics can’t be combined in a\nclever way to reconstruct peoples’ data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487430,
    "dDurationMs": 4069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But up through the 2010 census, the Census\nbureau couldn’t promise this - sure, they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491499,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were jittering data published in census bureau\ntables and charts, but not in a mathematically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495599,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rigorous way, and so the Census bureau couldn’t\nmathematically promise anything about how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499619,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much they were protecting our privacy (or\nsay how badly it’s been violated)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503619,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Until now!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504619,
    "dDurationMs": 5571,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The US 2020 Census will, for the first time,\nbe using mathematically rigorous privacy protections."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510190,
    "dDurationMs": 3529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the biggest benefits of the mathematically\nrigorous definition of privacy is that it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513719,
    "dDurationMs": 3565,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reliably compounds over multiple pieces of\ninformation - like, if we have a group of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517284,
    "dDurationMs": 4146,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people and publish both their average age\nand median age, each with a privacy loss factor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521430,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 3, then the privacy loss factor for having\nreleased both pieces of information is at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525710,
    "dDurationMs": 1010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most 6."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526720,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can decide on a total cumulative amount\nof privacy loss you’re willing to suffer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530570,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": ", and then decide whether you want to release,\nsay, 10 pieces of information each with 1/10th"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535520,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that total privacy loss (and less accuracy),\nor if you want to release 1 piece of information"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540070,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the full privacy loss and a higher level\nof accuracy.But how much privacy we need is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545010,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a really hard question to answer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547060,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, it involves weighing how much we as\nsociety collectively value the possible benefits"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551460,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from accurately knowing stuff about the group\nwe’re surveying vs the possible drawbacks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554170,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of releasing some amount of private information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556510,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And second, even though those benefits and\ndrawbacks can be mathematically measured as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560370,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“accuracy” and “privacy loss”, we\nstill have to translate the mathematical ideas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564120,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of “accuracy” and “privacy loss” into\nsomething that’s understandable and relatable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567640,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to people in our society."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568990,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s partly a goal of this video, in fact!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571410,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let’s give it one more shot at a translation.First\nand foremost: it is in principle impossible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576600,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to publish useful statistics based on private\ndata without in some way violating the privacy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581360,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the individuals in question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583220,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you want to provide a mathematically\nguaranteed limit on the amount of privacy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586610,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "violation, you have to randomly jitter the\nstatistics to protect the private data.The"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591010,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accuracy of the information after being jittered\nis generally described probabilistically,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594940,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by saying something like “if we randomly\njittered the true population of this town"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598790,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a bunch of times, 98% of the time our jittered\nstatistic would be within 10 people of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603180,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "true value.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604320,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So accuracy has two components: how close\nyou want your privacy-protected statistic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608220,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be to the real answer , and how likely\nit is to be that close."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612150,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The loss of privacy due to the publication\nof information is described in terms of how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616220,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "confidently an attacker would be able to single\nout a particular possibility for the true"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620540,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "data the plausibility of different possible\ntrue values for the underlying data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621540,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Given the published information, are there\njust a few possibilities for the true data?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624970,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or are there many, many, plausible possibilities\nfor what the true data might be?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 628730,
    "dDurationMs": 4850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Essentially, loss of privacy is measured by\nthe prominence of peaks on the plausibility"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633580,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634580,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so the protection of privacy requires\npolicing the possibility for such peaks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638280,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we individuals are going to willingly participate\nin scientific or other studies and surveys"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642270,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or use services where we reveal potentially\nsensitive personal information, we should"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646420,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really demand that the researchers or organizations\nutilize a mathematically robust way of protecting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650800,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our privacy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652050,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Simply put, if they can’t guarantee there\nwon’t be a peak in plausibility, then we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656620,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shouldn’t agree to give them a peek at our\ndata."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659920,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "SPONSORSHIP MESSAGE\nThanks to the U.S. Census Bureau for supporting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663530,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664530,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The founders of the US understood that an\naccurate and complete population count is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668250,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "necessary for the fair implementation of a\nrepresentative democracy, so a regular census"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672680,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is required by/enshrined in the US Constitution."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675010,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The US 2020 Census will be the first anywhere\nto use modern, mathematically guaranteed privacy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679660,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "safeguards to protect respondents from today’s\nprivacy threats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683100,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These new safeguards will protect confidentiality\nwhile allowing the Census Bureau to deliver"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686790,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the complete and accurate count of the nation’s\npopulation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689220,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They will also give those who rely on census\ndata increased clarity regarding the impact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693390,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that statistical safeguards have on their\nanalyses and decision-making."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696090,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In short, the Census Bureau views the adoption\nof a mathematical guarantee of privacy as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700720,
    "dDurationMs": 7550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a win-win.Here’s how the chief scientist\nat the Census bureau thinks about it: there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708270,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a real choice that every curator of confidential\nsurvey data has to make."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712450,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If they want the respondents to trust them\nto protect confidentiality, then the curator"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716270,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has to be prepared to give (and implement)\nmathematically provable guarantees of privacy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721070,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unfortunately, this means there’s a constraint\non the amount of information you can publish"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724280,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from confidential data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725770,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s mathematically impossible to provide\nperfectly accurate answers for as many questions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729830,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or statistics as you want while also protecting\nthe privacy of respondents."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733740,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So curators need to do two things: understand\nthe needs and desires of the people who provided"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737740,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "data and the people who want to use the data\nin order to determine precisely what balance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741370,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of accuracy vs privacy to choose, and then\nnot waste that limited privacy budget by publishing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746470,
    "dDurationMs": 2809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accurate answers to unimportant questions."
    } ]
  } ]
}
